---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const objects = await getCollection('objects', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
---

<Base title="Institute — Sekiya" description="What Sekiya is: an independent institute for computer science, mathematics and computational experimentation." objectCount={objects.length}>
  <header class="page-head shell">
    <p class="kicker">Institute</p>
    <h1>A reading room, switched on.</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">
      Sekiya is an independent institute for computer science, mathematics and computational
      experimentation. It exists for curiosity: elegant experiments, strange behaviour, complexity made
      visible, systems built simply to be understood. Serious mathematics and engineering —
      <em>without academic stiffness</em>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="institute-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Spirit</h3>
        <p>
          discover → experiment → understand → build → show
        </p>
        <p>
          A description of character, not a workflow. Nothing here passes through gates; a question is
          enough to begin.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Areas</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Models &amp; Statistics — model systems, estimators, learning and inference under change</li>
          <li>Systems &amp; Security — what a record can and cannot establish about what happened</li>
          <li>Agentic Systems — whether an agent's account of its work can be trusted</li>
          <li>Computation — deterministic, reproducible, inspectable computing</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Standards</h3>
        <p>
          Whatever a Sekiya study claims, the claim is earned: reproducible runs, stated limits, and
          results that say where they stop. Rigor is the infrastructure here — it is not the identity.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Standing work</h3>
        <p>
          Some instruments here are older than the institute's name and keep the public identity they
          were first published under &mdash;
          <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/trace-npm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">trace-npm</a>
          {' '}ships on npm under the name it always has. Object numbers carry over unchanged; a small
          <span class="mono mono-dim">origin</span> tag on those pages says where a piece of work began.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal">
        <h3>Elsewhere</h3>
        <p>
          <a href="https://joshuadefreitas.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Joshua de Freitas</a>
          &mdash; the founder's personal site. Sekiya is the research; everything else is somewhere else.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
